The benefits and agreements mentioned in subparagraphs (a) and (b) are set out in Annex IX. **Article 55 – Overlapping of benefits of a different kind** 1. If the receipt of benefits of a different kind or other income triggers the application of national rules designed to prevent overlapping, these provisions must be interpreted as follows:  
   (a) In relation to two or more independent benefits, the competent institutions shall prorate the benefit or benefits by dividing the amount or amounts received by the number of benefits subject to the restriction; however, this cannot be used to disqualify the recipient from the benefits covered under the other Chapters of this Title in accordance with the conditions and procedures laid down in the Implementing Regulation;  
   (b) In respect of one or more pro-rata benefits, the competent institutions must apply the rules to prevent overlapping by adjusting the benefit or other income in accordance with the ratio of the periods of insurance and/or residence as calculated in accordance with Article 52(1)(b)(ii)..

